1
00:00:01,141 --> 00:00:03,840
(Life Is Full of Variables)

2
00:00:03,841 --> 00:00:05,271
Nice to see you, everyone.

3
00:00:06,071 --> 00:00:07,911
- MINHO. - Yes.

4
00:00:08,111 --> 00:00:10,141
So our country actually acknowledged you...

5
00:00:10,511 --> 00:00:12,150
as the passionate and charismatic athlete.

6
00:00:12,151 --> 00:00:13,451
- What? - What's this about?

7
00:00:13,611 --> 00:00:16,051
- It's a huge honor for me. - Yes.

8
00:00:16,221 --> 00:00:18,650
I was appointed the honorary ambassador of KSOC.

9
00:00:18,651 --> 00:00:19,651
What?

10
00:00:19,652 --> 00:00:21,590
I'll be their honorary ambassador for two years.

11
00:00:21,591 --> 00:00:22,820
("MINHO Gets Appointed Honorary Ambassador")

12
00:00:22,821 --> 00:00:23,990
("MINHO, the New Face of KSOC")

13
00:00:23,991 --> 00:00:24,991
You're the perfect person for it.

14
00:00:24,991 --> 00:00:25,991
- Right. - Yes.

15
00:00:25,992 --> 00:00:27,700
- Only you can pull that off. - Exactly.

16
00:00:27,701 --> 00:00:28,730
- Yes. - What a positive appointment.

17
00:00:28,731 --> 00:00:30,461
- Congratulations. - Congratulations.

18
00:00:31,171 --> 00:00:32,200
- They picked the right guy. - With this momentum,

19
00:00:32,201 --> 00:00:33,470
- you'll exercise even more. - Yes.

20
00:00:33,471 --> 00:00:35,170
By the way, I really wanted to see you.

21
00:00:35,171 --> 00:00:36,171
- Me? - Why?

22
00:00:36,172 --> 00:00:38,071
Yes. You guys had the race last time I was here.

23
00:00:38,141 --> 00:00:39,210
- Oh, the race of the century? - I see. Right.

24
00:00:39,211 --> 00:00:40,570
You guys teased him a lot.

25
00:00:40,571 --> 00:00:41,581
It's totally going to work.

26
00:00:42,381 --> 00:00:44,280
(He went up against CODE KUNST in a soccer match...)

27
00:00:44,281 --> 00:00:46,280
(and lost.)

28
00:00:46,281 --> 00:00:48,320
(MINHO, you were supposed to give it a curve.)

29
00:00:48,321 --> 00:00:49,981
(And you were supposed to kick it with the back of your foot.)

30
00:00:50,181 --> 00:00:51,890
(Getting lectured from the two upset him more than the result.)

31
00:00:51,891 --> 00:00:53,721
(Gosh, you're frustrating.)

32
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:57,861
(He kindly demonstrated for MINHO out of frustration.)

33
00:00:58,831 --> 00:01:00,261
(This is how you do it.)

34
00:01:01,301 --> 00:01:03,531
(MINHO, I ought to help you polish your skills.)

35
00:01:04,231 --> 00:01:06,901
Here's what I really loved about MINHO.

36
00:01:07,501 --> 00:01:10,370
After Hyun Moo and I gave you a few tips on playing soccer,

37
00:01:10,371 --> 00:01:11,440
- Yes. - I...

38
00:01:11,441 --> 00:01:13,740
- watched him play soccer. - Okay.

39
00:01:13,741 --> 00:01:16,111
Your movements definitely got smoother.

40
00:01:17,011 --> 00:01:18,380
- So... - We had an influence on him.

41
00:01:18,381 --> 00:01:19,750
- Let me explain. - Our theoretical knowledge is good.

42
00:01:19,751 --> 00:01:21,720
- We'll have a sports day. - Yes.

43
00:01:21,721 --> 00:01:23,250
- You must come as Iron Man. - Yes.

44
00:01:23,251 --> 00:01:24,590
- It won't be complete without you. - Right.

45
00:01:24,591 --> 00:01:25,921
And we'll be teamed up together.

46
00:01:26,251 --> 00:01:28,561
- Come on. Let's do a handshake. - He's pulling away.

47
00:01:29,191 --> 00:01:30,191
(In a hurry)

48
00:01:30,192 --> 00:01:32,491
- Hold on. Are there already teams? - Wait. What are the teams?

49
00:01:32,691 --> 00:01:33,990
Innocent Moo and Ku Sports Day...

50
00:01:33,991 --> 00:01:35,430
- is the name. - Yes.

51
00:01:35,431 --> 00:01:37,230
- There are Team Moo and Team Ku. - Team Moo and Team Ku.

52
00:01:37,231 --> 00:01:38,701
- Team Moo and Team Ku. - Team Moo...

53
00:01:38,831 --> 00:01:42,100
And I want you on my team, MINHO.

54
00:01:42,101 --> 00:01:44,541
- Are you recruiting him now? - Oh, my.

55
00:01:44,971 --> 00:01:46,540
This is the recruiting battle.

56
00:01:46,541 --> 00:01:48,840
You know what? I taught you a few tips and so on.

57
00:01:48,841 --> 00:01:51,481
If MINHO joins your team, I'll follow him.

58
00:01:51,581 --> 00:01:52,781
- Yes. - This is nice.

59
00:01:53,511 --> 00:01:55,480
- I'm the team captain. - No.

60
00:01:55,481 --> 00:01:57,250
We should all be on Team MINHO.

61
00:01:57,251 --> 00:01:59,421
- Yes, let's be on Team MINHO. Yes. - We'll be on Team MINHO.

62
00:01:59,591 --> 00:02:02,460
The rest of the guests will join Team Hyun Moo.

63
00:02:02,461 --> 00:02:03,721
Kian84, I want you on my team.

64
00:02:04,061 --> 00:02:05,560
- Me? - I need at least you.

65
00:02:05,561 --> 00:02:07,191
I don't want to join neither.

66
00:02:07,601 --> 00:02:08,660
- Join him. - Come on.

67
00:02:08,661 --> 00:02:10,330
- My gosh, seriously. - You're being mean.

68
00:02:10,331 --> 00:02:12,571
Just pretend that there are no team captains.

69
00:02:12,671 --> 00:02:14,140
In the end, you'll have to play rock-paper-scissors...

70
00:02:14,141 --> 00:02:15,170
- and pick. - Right.

71
00:02:15,171 --> 00:02:16,770
- I thought you were confident. - Yes. Of course.

72
00:02:16,771 --> 00:02:17,971
Rock-paper-scissors.

73
00:02:18,311 --> 00:02:19,371
MINHO.

74
00:02:21,581 --> 00:02:23,710
(He's unstoppable.)

75
00:02:23,711 --> 00:02:25,250
- Here's what's important. - Yes.

76
00:02:25,251 --> 00:02:27,550
You guys don't know what kind of sport we'll play.

77
00:02:27,551 --> 00:02:29,680
- We're working on that now. - I see.

78
00:02:29,681 --> 00:02:31,090
Are there prizes too?

79
00:02:31,091 --> 00:02:32,290
- There are. - Really?

80
00:02:32,291 --> 00:02:33,590
Yes, I'll spend some money.

81
00:02:33,591 --> 00:02:34,620
(Spoken like old money)

82
00:02:34,621 --> 00:02:36,760
- Chairman Jun. - This will motivate us to play.

83
00:02:36,761 --> 00:02:39,260
- We'll be playing real sports. - My gosh.

84
00:02:39,261 --> 00:02:40,660
- I love that. - This is great.

85
00:02:40,661 --> 00:02:42,430
I'll come up with the sports day...

86
00:02:42,431 --> 00:02:44,471
that will satisfy even the honorary ambassador.

87
00:02:44,671 --> 00:02:46,471
- I'll be looking forward to it. - Yes.

88
00:02:48,071 --> 00:02:49,840
(Being Handsome Is Torture)

89
00:02:49,841 --> 00:02:51,240
- "Being Handsome Is Torture?" - What's that?

90
00:02:51,241 --> 00:02:52,471
"Being Handsome Is Torture."

91
00:02:54,911 --> 00:02:58,251
(Sung Hwan is trudging along in the pouring rain.)

92
00:02:59,851 --> 00:03:01,250
Look at your knee.

93
00:03:01,251 --> 00:03:02,280
It still hasn't healed.

94
00:03:02,281 --> 00:03:03,950
That was after the race with Hyun Moo.

95
00:03:03,951 --> 00:03:05,720
- It still hasn't healed? - No.

96
00:03:05,721 --> 00:03:06,790
It's a different wound.

97
00:03:06,791 --> 00:03:10,321
I was practicing action scenes and then hurt myself.

98
00:03:10,491 --> 00:03:12,460
Did the race affect your training?

99
00:03:12,461 --> 00:03:14,261
I hurt my left knee then, but that's my right knee.

100
00:03:15,231 --> 00:03:16,830
Both of your knees were destroyed.

101
00:03:16,831 --> 00:03:17,870
They were totally destroyed.

102
00:03:17,871 --> 00:03:19,200
- The injury is all over his body. - Both of them were injured.

103
00:03:19,201 --> 00:03:20,330
Both of his legs were injured.

104
00:03:20,331 --> 00:03:22,040
Sung Hwan, you should sit out the sports day.

105
00:03:22,041 --> 00:03:23,070
- Right. - Yes.

106
00:03:23,071 --> 00:03:24,310
How can you play with injured legs?

107
00:03:24,311 --> 00:03:26,210
- I'm doing physical therapy now. - Sung Hwan.

108
00:03:26,211 --> 00:03:27,370
Let's just do the fan dance.

109
00:03:27,371 --> 00:03:28,881
- Yes. Let's do that. - What race? Seriously.

110
00:03:31,711 --> 00:03:33,551
(Pouring)

111
00:03:34,981 --> 00:03:36,581
My gosh, why is it pouring today?

112
00:03:39,821 --> 00:03:41,861
(Shaking)

113
00:03:43,861 --> 00:03:46,191
Your shoulders are so broad that one of your shoulders got wet.

114
00:03:46,531 --> 00:03:47,730
I loved how you put it.

115
00:03:47,731 --> 00:03:48,731
(Satisfied)

116
00:03:49,801 --> 00:03:52,531
(He arrives at a place with a wet shoulder.)

117
00:03:54,031 --> 00:03:56,041
(Checking his face)

118
00:03:58,711 --> 00:04:00,140
My goodness.

119
00:04:00,141 --> 00:04:01,810
- How handsome. - Yes.

120
00:04:01,811 --> 00:04:02,911
What a handsome face from every angle.

121
00:04:03,741 --> 00:04:05,551
- This is driving me crazy. - What?

122
00:04:05,651 --> 00:04:06,981
- Is it about hair loss? - No.

123
00:04:07,381 --> 00:04:08,820
- Physical therapy for your knees? - No.

124
00:04:08,821 --> 00:04:09,951
(Laughing)

125
00:04:10,651 --> 00:04:11,691
Let's go.

126
00:04:11,891 --> 00:04:13,020
Going up.

127
00:04:13,021 --> 00:04:14,121
Where are you going?

128
00:04:14,491 --> 00:04:15,491
(Exhaling)

129
00:04:16,191 --> 00:04:17,561
The doors are opening.

130
00:04:17,761 --> 00:04:20,631
(He arrives while feeling anxious.)

131
00:04:22,901 --> 00:04:24,770
- It must be a dermatology clinic. - Right.

132
00:04:24,771 --> 00:04:25,900
- Hello. - Hello.

133
00:04:25,901 --> 00:04:27,431
- It's a clinic. - Hello.

134
00:04:28,301 --> 00:04:30,071
(Pressing)

135
00:04:30,201 --> 00:04:32,110
I've registered you. You can wait for a bit.

136
00:04:32,111 --> 00:04:33,171
Okay.

137
00:04:34,411 --> 00:04:37,111
(He's registered into a mysterious system.)

138
00:04:39,451 --> 00:04:41,781
(Chuckling)

139
00:04:42,821 --> 00:04:44,721
(Hold on.)

140
00:04:45,091 --> 00:04:47,151
This looks familiar.

141
00:04:47,351 --> 00:04:48,360
- What? - This...

142
00:04:48,361 --> 00:04:49,361
(This looks familiar for some reason.)

143
00:04:49,861 --> 00:04:51,730
(It was seen at Moomoo's house.)

144
00:04:51,731 --> 00:04:52,791
"The Martian."

145
00:04:53,561 --> 00:04:54,830
(Abundant nature)

146
00:04:54,831 --> 00:04:56,000
I told you it'd be at a subway station...

147
00:04:56,001 --> 00:04:57,801
- or a dermatology clinic. - My gosh.

148
00:04:58,401 --> 00:04:59,470
- It's the same thing. - It looks exactly the same.

149
00:04:59,471 --> 00:05:00,670
They must be managed by the same agency.

150
00:05:00,671 --> 00:05:02,170
- I guess we use the same agency. - Right.

151
00:05:02,171 --> 00:05:03,871
- The same agency? - That's not important.

152
00:05:04,071 --> 00:05:05,740
No one has that at home.

153
00:05:05,741 --> 00:05:08,411
- Who would have that at their home? - Exactly.

154
00:05:08,511 --> 00:05:10,210
When I saw it, I thought I was at your house.

155
00:05:10,211 --> 00:05:11,951
Right. It's the interior design of a lobby.

156
00:05:12,551 --> 00:05:14,551
Hyun Moo likes this kind of thing.

157
00:05:15,521 --> 00:05:17,751
Gosh, he and I can't ever mix.

158
00:05:18,391 --> 00:05:19,551
You just don't mix well.

159
00:05:19,691 --> 00:05:22,361
(He sits down while feeling Moomoo's energy.)

160
00:05:23,461 --> 00:05:24,590
All right.

161
00:05:24,591 --> 00:05:25,591
(Let's see.)

162
00:05:28,731 --> 00:05:31,871
(He's checking his face again.)

163
00:05:32,871 --> 00:05:34,941
How unfortunate.

164
00:05:36,071 --> 00:05:38,471
I should have come sooner. But I've been putting it off.

165
00:05:38,971 --> 00:05:41,981
I came to a hospital because of vitiligo.

166
00:05:42,411 --> 00:05:43,681
- Really? - I see.

167
00:05:44,351 --> 00:05:46,081
The discoloration was getting wider.

168
00:05:48,951 --> 00:05:51,150
(He always applied sunscreen...)

169
00:05:51,151 --> 00:05:53,351
(that turned his skin whiter than that of Kkotbun.)

170
00:05:54,191 --> 00:05:56,021
(There was a reason behind that.)

171
00:05:56,261 --> 00:05:58,591
(A few years ago, I filmed a movie in Kazakhstan with Ju Seung.)

172
00:05:59,831 --> 00:06:03,660
(Afterward, his vitiligo has gotten worse.)

173
00:06:03,661 --> 00:06:05,031
- Because of the sun. - Yes.

174
00:06:05,331 --> 00:06:08,001
(My doctor told me to apply a lot of sunscreen.)

175
00:06:08,101 --> 00:06:11,000
(He always relied on sunscreen.)

176
00:06:11,001 --> 00:06:13,211
- You began applying it generously. - Yes.

177
00:06:13,571 --> 00:06:15,610
Actually, I apply a lot more when I go out.

178
00:06:15,611 --> 00:06:16,880
- You should. - I apply it on my neck too.

179
00:06:16,881 --> 00:06:19,681
But I went to the beach this summer.

180
00:06:19,781 --> 00:06:21,520
Only the discolored patches didn't get tanned.

181
00:06:21,521 --> 00:06:23,181
- So it looks worse now. - Gosh.

182
00:06:23,521 --> 00:06:24,920
- That must be so stressful. - It's not like...

183
00:06:24,921 --> 00:06:26,350
you can cover up the patches.

184
00:06:26,351 --> 00:06:27,650
You're an actor too.

185
00:06:27,651 --> 00:06:28,990
- Right. It must be... - Your face is on TV all the time.

186
00:06:28,991 --> 00:06:30,361
- so stressful. - This must be stressful.

187
00:06:31,331 --> 00:06:33,830
When I'm on TV, the viewers can't see the patches...

188
00:06:33,831 --> 00:06:36,701
because I cover them up with makeup.

189
00:06:37,001 --> 00:06:38,300
- I'm not wearing any makeup now. - My gosh.

190
00:06:38,301 --> 00:06:39,570
- I'm not sure if you can see them. - Right.

191
00:06:39,571 --> 00:06:40,730
You can see them on my eyebrow,

192
00:06:40,731 --> 00:06:42,501
- My gosh. - nose, and mouth.

193
00:06:42,741 --> 00:06:44,911
- Oh, no. - They're all over my face.

194
00:06:45,311 --> 00:06:47,371
I'm getting more patches now.

195
00:06:47,711 --> 00:06:49,010
It's not that I don't have any eyebrows.

196
00:06:49,011 --> 00:06:50,311
It got decolored and became white.

197
00:06:50,611 --> 00:06:52,181
- I see. - That's pretty serious.

198
00:06:52,911 --> 00:06:54,420
All of the facial hair will turn white.

199
00:06:54,421 --> 00:06:55,551
- Really? - I see.

200
00:06:55,881 --> 00:06:57,051
It sounds like a serious condition.

201
00:06:57,621 --> 00:07:00,591
I got tested in May.

202
00:07:01,161 --> 00:07:02,621
The doctor was surprised...

203
00:07:03,391 --> 00:07:06,731
and brought in the nurses and the chief nurse.

204
00:07:06,831 --> 00:07:08,861
Afterward, this condition began to stress me.

205
00:07:09,001 --> 00:07:11,670
I was wondering if this condition could improve.

206
00:07:11,671 --> 00:07:13,601
That's why I'm here on my day off.

207
00:07:13,971 --> 00:07:16,171
- You must get treated for it. - Sung Hwan, is it possible?

208
00:07:16,241 --> 00:07:17,840
Can it improve with the right treatment?

209
00:07:17,841 --> 00:07:19,910
Actually, the thing with vitiligo is...

210
00:07:19,911 --> 00:07:22,441
- there's no cure. - Right. It will be difficult.

211
00:07:22,581 --> 00:07:24,810
If you don't take precautions, the patches could widen again?

212
00:07:24,811 --> 00:07:27,050
That's why I've been going to the clinic often.

213
00:07:27,051 --> 00:07:28,521
- To prevent them from getting big? - I see.

214
00:07:30,651 --> 00:07:31,890
(This isn't his first time here.)

215
00:07:31,891 --> 00:07:33,391
Gosh, why am I nervous?

216
00:07:35,991 --> 00:07:38,130
Sung Hwan, let's get you prepared.

217
00:07:38,131 --> 00:07:39,160
Okay.

218
00:07:39,161 --> 00:07:40,261
(Getting up)

219
00:07:40,791 --> 00:07:42,000
Please put on the gown...

220
00:07:42,001 --> 00:07:44,231
- and change your shoes. - Okay.

221
00:07:44,631 --> 00:07:45,771
(Men's Dressing Room)

222
00:07:46,571 --> 00:07:48,941
(He enters the washroom after getting changed.)

223
00:07:50,341 --> 00:07:52,841
(He's ready to wash his face after putting on a cute headband.)

224
00:07:54,981 --> 00:07:56,180
That's quite a face.

225
00:07:56,181 --> 00:07:57,311
(I know it's my face and all, but that's quite a face.)

226
00:07:58,311 --> 00:07:59,981
Gosh, it makes me shy to wash my face there.

227
00:08:00,151 --> 00:08:01,681
- You have to, though. - Yes.

228
00:08:02,051 --> 00:08:03,951
Because the doctor must see your bare face to diagnose?

229
00:08:04,121 --> 00:08:06,291
- They tell you to wash your face. - You must wash up completely.

230
00:08:10,291 --> 00:08:11,691
- My goodness. - Gosh.

231
00:08:13,031 --> 00:08:14,431
- My goodness. - Gosh.

232
00:08:14,961 --> 00:08:16,031
That's my habit.

233
00:08:17,901 --> 00:08:20,001
(Glancing)

234
00:08:21,601 --> 00:08:22,771
- Oh, no. - My gosh.

235
00:08:23,041 --> 00:08:25,311
(He realizes something went wrong.)

236
00:08:26,941 --> 00:08:28,480
(He quickly tries to wipe them with his hand.)

237
00:08:28,481 --> 00:08:30,111
(A quick glance)

238
00:08:32,381 --> 00:08:33,681
I cleaned it.

239
00:08:34,851 --> 00:08:35,880
(He thoroughly wipes the mirror.)

240
00:08:35,881 --> 00:08:37,251
You can just wipe it.

241
00:08:39,521 --> 00:08:40,591
My gosh.

242
00:08:41,621 --> 00:08:44,391
(I forgot to wash my face. Only the mirror is clean.)

243
00:08:45,191 --> 00:08:47,291
(Thoroughly washing)

244
00:08:48,661 --> 00:08:49,760
You took a shower in there.

245
00:08:49,761 --> 00:08:51,530
(He dries the mirror at the end.)

246
00:08:51,531 --> 00:08:52,601
Okay.

247
00:08:53,631 --> 00:08:54,700
All done.

248
00:08:54,701 --> 00:08:56,300
(His face and mirror are both clean.)

249
00:08:56,301 --> 00:08:57,470
- Are you done? - Yes.

250
00:08:57,471 --> 00:08:58,970
- Then... - Okay.

251
00:08:58,971 --> 00:09:01,980
You'll use Meta-Vu, the skin analyzer.

252
00:09:01,981 --> 00:09:05,111
Put your head in all the way. Great.

253
00:09:06,881 --> 00:09:09,081
- With that device, you can see... - It captures everything?

254
00:09:09,221 --> 00:09:10,581
All the discolored patches.

255
00:09:10,921 --> 00:09:12,421
- I didn't know about this device. - Yes.

256
00:09:16,821 --> 00:09:18,761
- You look like a baby again. - My gosh.

257
00:09:19,091 --> 00:09:20,790
- You're a baby. - Let's skip this part.

258
00:09:20,791 --> 00:09:21,960
- He looks like a baby. - Yes.

