- That looks even more bizarre. - My gosh.

520
00:19:20,174 --> 00:19:21,443
(Shocked)

521
00:19:21,444 --> 00:19:23,344
- He was in "Toy Story." - This is...

522
00:19:23,884 --> 00:19:25,384
- He looks like a cartoon character. - Look!

523
00:19:26,054 --> 00:19:27,454
- He looks like a cartoon character. - Look!

524
00:19:27,654 --> 00:19:29,183
It looks like he's in space too.

525
00:19:29,184 --> 00:19:31,324
An alien is here to conquer our planet.

526
00:19:31,554 --> 00:19:32,694
To conquer our planet?

527
00:19:33,694 --> 00:19:35,223
(The conqueror from space is coming after our planet.)

528
00:19:35,224 --> 00:19:36,564
Why are you smiling?

529
00:19:37,064 --> 00:19:38,494
But he looks like a kind alien.

530
00:19:39,134 --> 00:19:40,233
- Set that as your profile picture. - Are you all right?

531
00:19:40,234 --> 00:19:41,234
Yes.

532
00:19:43,734 --> 00:19:45,474
The alien is smiling subtly.

533
00:19:46,374 --> 00:19:47,403
- It's like he's dreaming... - He looks like an alien.

534
00:19:47,404 --> 00:19:48,443
Of conquering our planet...

535
00:19:48,444 --> 00:19:50,004
- on the spaceship. - Yes.

536
00:19:51,714 --> 00:19:55,284
(Comfortable)

537
00:19:56,784 --> 00:19:57,984
I'll remove this.

538
00:19:58,284 --> 00:20:00,523
She didn't laugh at him, though.

539
00:20:00,524 --> 00:20:01,754
I go there often.

540
00:20:03,084 --> 00:20:05,854
(She applies sunscreen on him as if she had done this many times.)

541
00:20:07,224 --> 00:20:08,494
Did it stop raining?

542
00:20:08,924 --> 00:20:11,094
They apply a lot of sunscreen after the treatment.

543
00:20:11,494 --> 00:20:12,934
- You're all set. - Thank you.

544
00:20:16,964 --> 00:20:18,703
- Good job hanging in there. - Thank you.

545
00:20:18,704 --> 00:20:20,274
- That must've been tough. - Okay.

546
00:20:20,844 --> 00:20:22,403
- I had been putting it off. - Okay. Thank you.

547
00:20:22,404 --> 00:20:24,514
So when I was there, I felt relieved.

548
00:20:25,474 --> 00:20:26,474
I'm glad you went.

549
00:20:29,644 --> 00:20:31,413
- Thank you. Have a good day. - Thank you.

550
00:20:31,414 --> 00:20:32,484
Thanks. Bye.

551
00:20:33,554 --> 00:20:35,383
(He strides out of the pharmacy.)

552
00:20:35,384 --> 00:20:36,454
There it is.

553
00:20:37,854 --> 00:20:40,524
(He called a taxi in advance.)

554
00:20:43,394 --> 00:20:45,094
(Exhausted from the surgery...)

555
00:20:45,994 --> 00:20:47,534
- Hello. - Hello.

556
00:20:47,904 --> 00:20:50,204
(He quickly heads out.)

557
00:20:52,074 --> 00:20:53,403
(Looking full of worry)

558
00:20:53,404 --> 00:20:55,173
I was so stressed.

559
00:20:55,174 --> 00:20:56,703
When you go to clinics for health reasons,

560
00:20:56,704 --> 00:20:58,714
- those visits feel like homework. - And...

561
00:20:59,044 --> 00:21:01,213
(Samgakji Station)

562
00:21:01,214 --> 00:21:02,544
I wonder where he's going next.

563
00:21:02,644 --> 00:21:03,783
He'll probably eat something.

564
00:21:03,784 --> 00:21:05,984
Right. For sure.

565
00:21:06,954 --> 00:21:08,754
Since he has vitiligo, he'll get a dish starting with V.

566
00:21:09,684 --> 00:21:11,093
- That will be his excuse. - Right.

567
00:21:11,094 --> 00:21:12,154
It's raining.

568
00:21:12,754 --> 00:21:13,754
Have a good day.

569
00:21:13,755 --> 00:21:14,794
(He arrives at a place after the treatment.)

570
00:21:15,564 --> 00:21:16,693
Gosh, this is nice.

571
00:21:16,694 --> 00:21:18,794
- He's in Itaewon. - I'm hungry.

572
00:21:20,394 --> 00:21:21,434
(Itaewon)

573
00:21:24,434 --> 00:21:26,274
I have an English name, Marcus.

574
00:21:26,674 --> 00:21:28,003
I was exposed to the American culture...

575
00:21:28,004 --> 00:21:29,344
ever since I was a kid.

576
00:21:29,504 --> 00:21:32,443
In 2003, I lived in Itaewon...

577
00:21:32,444 --> 00:21:34,544
for a year.

578
00:21:35,044 --> 00:21:36,143
Really?

579
00:21:36,144 --> 00:21:37,613
Yes. I lived at my friend's house...

580
00:21:37,614 --> 00:21:39,013
when I performed in children's plays.

581
00:21:39,014 --> 00:21:40,723
I lived with him for a year.

582
00:21:40,724 --> 00:21:42,054
("The Tale of Sim Cheong")

583
00:21:42,084 --> 00:21:45,124
From 2010 to 2015,

584
00:21:45,294 --> 00:21:48,094
I used to come here on Thursday, Friday, and Saturday.

585
00:21:48,324 --> 00:21:51,294
That's how much I love the culture in Itaewon.

586
00:21:51,564 --> 00:21:54,764
I would say Itaewon is my fifth hometown.

587
00:21:54,904 --> 00:21:56,203
You have a lot of hometowns.

588
00:21:56,204 --> 00:21:57,774
(You have five hometowns?)

589
00:21:58,074 --> 00:21:59,874
My gosh, it smells good.

590
00:22:01,204 --> 00:22:02,574
Excuse me.

591
00:22:04,544 --> 00:22:07,214
(He starts speaking in English now that he's in his hometown.)

592
00:22:09,744 --> 00:22:11,583
(He naturally heads into a burger place.)

593
00:22:11,584 --> 00:22:13,254
- You love burgers. - I love burgers.

594
00:22:14,454 --> 00:22:16,724
- That's Marcus indeed. - Hello.

595
00:22:16,884 --> 00:22:17,924
Yes.

596
00:22:19,354 --> 00:22:21,124
(Exuding the American vibe)

597
00:22:21,964 --> 00:22:23,423
As for the restaurant I visited today,

598
00:22:23,424 --> 00:22:25,393
that's my go-to spot when I'm stressed.

599
00:22:25,394 --> 00:22:28,434
It's my soulmate that can comfort me.

600
00:22:28,634 --> 00:22:30,903
It was the dish I wanted the most when I was stressed.

601
00:22:30,904 --> 00:22:33,134
I hated how painful it was. So I went...

602
00:22:33,404 --> 00:22:34,604
to an authentic American place.

603
00:22:35,074 --> 00:22:37,413
I went to have an authentic American burger.

604
00:22:37,414 --> 00:22:38,443
You need a reward.

605
00:22:38,444 --> 00:22:39,743
I'm salivating.

606
00:22:39,744 --> 00:22:41,284
(He's here for a comforting meal after a hard day.)

607
00:22:41,684 --> 00:22:42,684
- Hello. - My gosh.

608
00:22:42,685 --> 00:22:44,254
The Korean workers aren't here today.

609
00:22:45,184 --> 00:22:47,554
(He hesitates after seeing a non-Korean worker.)

610
00:22:48,324 --> 00:22:49,583
- Hi. - Hi.

611
00:22:49,584 --> 00:22:52,524
Well, the menu is...

612
00:22:52,994 --> 00:22:56,463
only at the kiosk?

613
00:22:56,464 --> 00:22:57,993
Yes. You have to order from there.

614
00:22:57,994 --> 00:22:59,563
The best burger is the deluxe burger.

615
00:22:59,564 --> 00:23:01,163
So you can try that one.

616
00:23:01,164 --> 00:23:02,334
- Yes. - Okay. Thank you.

617
00:23:03,204 --> 00:23:05,033
I don't know what she said.

618
00:23:05,034 --> 00:23:06,504
He thanked her when he didn't understand her.

619
00:23:08,544 --> 00:23:09,803
He cut her off before she could speak more.

620
00:23:09,804 --> 00:23:11,274
Right. "Thank you."

621
00:23:12,774 --> 00:23:13,814
A cheeseburger.

622
00:23:16,044 --> 00:23:17,683
As long as you don't eat any fritters...

623
00:23:17,684 --> 00:23:19,283
- Right. Just don't eat the fries. - Seriously. Yes.

624
00:23:19,284 --> 00:23:21,454
- It's the perfect meal. - It's great.

625
00:23:21,654 --> 00:23:23,083
- You're spot on. - It's the perfect meal.

626
00:23:23,084 --> 00:23:24,153
He's getting three burgers.

627
00:23:24,154 --> 00:23:25,523
But getting three would be a different story.

628
00:23:25,524 --> 00:23:26,593
What? What's this?

629
00:23:26,594 --> 00:23:27,823
- He ordered three burgers. - Gosh.

630
00:23:27,824 --> 00:23:29,563
- And he ordered sugar-free Coke. - He ordered three burgers.

631
00:23:29,564 --> 00:23:30,733
- Their burgers are great. - Just eat the fries...

632
00:23:30,734 --> 00:23:31,833
and have only one burger.

633
00:23:31,834 --> 00:23:33,394
No. I can't do that. My conscience won't allow it.

634
00:23:33,634 --> 00:23:34,734
Three?

635
00:23:35,964 --> 00:23:38,504
(He orders three burgers which are perfectly balanced.)

636
00:23:39,204 --> 00:23:40,804
- Excuse me. - Yes.

637
00:23:41,844 --> 00:23:44,343
Romaine and tomatoes. Outside.

638
00:23:44,344 --> 00:23:45,544
- Okay. - Okay?

639
00:23:45,614 --> 00:23:47,513
- Ippai sauce... - Yes.

640
00:23:47,514 --> 00:23:49,444
- Many... - What?

641
00:23:50,114 --> 00:23:52,584
(Ippai? Many?)

642
00:23:53,154 --> 00:23:55,054
(He perfectly speaks 2 languages.)

643
00:23:55,524 --> 00:23:56,853
"Can you add a lot of it?"

644
00:23:56,854 --> 00:23:58,154
(He just wanted a lot of sauce.)

645
00:23:58,854 --> 00:24:00,193
- Yes. - Ippai sauce...

646
00:24:00,194 --> 00:24:02,393
- Many... Dip a lot. Okay? - You want a lot of sauce?

647
00:24:02,394 --> 00:24:04,263
- Okay. Thank you. - All right.

648
00:24:04,264 --> 00:24:05,734
(He customized his order by using 3 languages.)

649
00:24:07,094 --> 00:24:09,404
(It will wash away the pain from the treatment.)

650
00:24:10,634 --> 00:24:12,103
It's so greasy.

651
00:24:12,104 --> 00:24:13,374
(Looking glossy)

652
00:24:16,844 --> 00:24:18,574
The smell is driving me crazy.

653
00:24:21,644 --> 00:24:23,344
(He gets up as the smell makes it impossible to stay still.)

654
00:24:23,584 --> 00:24:24,614
Is my order not ready yet?

655
00:24:27,214 --> 00:24:28,423
- Excuse me. - Yes.

656
00:24:28,424 --> 00:24:31,853
You speak Korean and English?

657
00:24:31,854 --> 00:24:33,024
I mean, you speak Korean?

658
00:24:33,124 --> 00:24:36,123
- Yes, I can speak Korean. - You can?

659
00:24:36,124 --> 00:24:37,493
Her pronunciation is better than yours.

660
00:24:37,494 --> 00:24:38,633
- Her pronunciation is better. - My gosh.

661
00:24:38,634 --> 00:24:40,093
- This is the deluxe burger. - The deluxe burger.

662
00:24:40,094 --> 00:24:42,234
This one is the cheeseburger. And this is the chicken burger.

663
00:24:42,504 --> 00:24:43,903
- As you requested, - I see.

664
00:24:43,904 --> 00:24:45,273
I didn't add any lettuce or tomatoes.

665
00:24:45,274 --> 00:24:46,404
What? You speak such good Korean!

666
00:24:47,004 --> 00:24:50,273
She thought I was one of the foreign customers.

667
00:24:50,274 --> 00:24:52,073
So she didn't speak Korean to me.

668
00:24:52,074 --> 00:24:54,743
- They get foreign customers too. - She thought you were Marcus.

669
00:24:54,744 --> 00:24:56,214
Gosh, this is so embarrassing.

670
00:24:57,084 --> 00:24:59,614
(He quickly goes to his table.)

671
00:25:00,514 --> 00:25:02,284
(The trio of burgers chosen by Marcus)

672
00:25:03,524 --> 00:25:05,254
(He solemnly puts on plastic gloves.)

673
00:25:06,524 --> 00:25:08,323
Calm down.

674
00:25:08,324 --> 00:25:10,094
- Calm down. - They always have black pepper.

675
00:25:10,464 --> 00:25:11,834
- You must sprinkle some pepper. - Oh, my.

676
00:25:12,764 --> 00:25:14,764
- There you go. - Hey.

677
00:25:14,934 --> 00:25:16,304
- Gosh. - Black pepper.

678
00:25:19,204 --> 00:25:21,343
He's sprinkling it on everything. Look at him coughing.

679
00:25:21,344 --> 00:25:22,604
Of course, it makes me cough.

680
00:25:25,074 --> 00:25:26,344
This is a solemn moment.

681
00:25:27,074 --> 00:25:29,214
(Pressing)

682
00:25:30,044 --> 00:25:31,313
Why are you pressing it?

683
00:25:31,314 --> 00:25:33,113
So I can get a nice bite of it.

684
00:25:33,114 --> 00:25:34,924
(He presses down on the burger and then takes a bite.)

685
00:25:36,554 --> 00:25:37,554
(Humming)

686
00:25:38,994 --> 00:25:40,624
Gosh, that's really tasty.

687
00:25:41,894 --> 00:25:43,694
(He keeps on biting into his comfort food.)

688
00:25:46,494 --> 00:25:47,833
Gosh, this is crazy.

689
00:25:47,834 --> 00:25:49,804
(It's washing away all of my stress.)

690
00:25:51,574 --> 00:25:52,574
(Approving)

691
00:25:54,844 --> 00:25:56,603
He eats so neatly.

692
00:25:56,604 --> 00:25:57,844
Nothing is spilling over.

693
00:25:58,574 --> 00:26:00,644
Look at that. How neat was that?

694
00:26:01,044 --> 00:26:03,413
He finished that in 3 to 4 bites.

695
00:26:03,414 --> 00:26:04,854
He finished that so quickly like it was a macaron.

696
00:26:07,184 --> 00:26:08,953
- He really eats it like a macaron. - Seriously.

697
00:26:08,954 --> 00:26:10,754
(Given the speed, he's having his second macaron.)

698
00:26:12,824 --> 00:26:15,994
(He's utterly captivated by his favorite food.)

699
00:26:18,064 --> 00:26:20,163
- I think you're eating too fast. - Right.

700
00:26:20,164 --> 00:26:22,303
- I'm trying to fix that. - Right. You need to chew more.

701
00:26:22,304 --> 00:26:23,334
Right.

702
00:26:28,344 --> 00:26:30,244
You're eating like it's a food competition.

703
00:26:30,674 --> 00:26:32,313
Is it because you felt empty inside? What were you feeling?

704
00:26:32,314 --> 00:26:35,083
That day, I just wanted to gorge on my favorite food...

705
00:26:35,084 --> 00:26:36,213
because I was so stressed.

706
00:26:36,214 --> 00:26:38,453
I don't eat when I'm really full...

707
00:26:38,454 --> 00:26:39,454
because I wouldn't feel good.

708
00:26:39,455 --> 00:26:40,824
- It's the same with everyone. - Really?

709
00:26:41,224 --> 00:26:42,623
- I... - Everyone stops eating then.

710
00:26:42,624 --> 00:26:43,624
(That's normal.)

711
00:26:46,554 --> 00:26:47,963
(Since he's not full, he grabs the last burger.)

712
00:26:47,964 --> 00:26:50,894
You're eating all three burgers without a sip of the Coke.

713
00:26:50,964 --> 00:26:52,864
There's a moment when I drink Coke.

714
00:26:53,164 --> 00:26:55,004
I drink it when I feel full.

715
00:26:56,334 --> 00:26:57,904
You don't drink it throughout the meal.

716
00:26:57,974 --> 00:26:59,834
- I guess he has his own rule. - I do.

717
00:27:00,904 --> 00:27:02,944
(A solo performance of the burger without the Coke)

718
00:27:06,674 --> 00:27:08,883
- Did he finish all three? - Gosh, that was so fast.

719
00:27:08,884 --> 00:27:11,114
- He's drinking it now. - I think it only took five minutes.

720
00:27:12,414 --> 00:27:13,783
(He finally gulps down the Coke.)

721
00:27:13,784 --> 00:27:17,254
And I must drink soda until my throat hurts.

722
00:27:17,424 --> 00:27:18,693
After that, he always says...

723
00:27:18,694 --> 00:27:19,954
- he has reflux esophagitis. - Right.

724
00:27:20,894 --> 00:27:22,394
I still take a lot of medicine.

725
00:27:23,964 --> 00:27:25,664
(But he washes down his stress.)

726
00:27:26,894 --> 00:27:28,204
I'm on a diet now.

727
00:27:28,534 --> 00:27:30,734
So I only ate about 70 percent of my usual meal.

728
00:27:31,004 --> 00:27:33,834
I need to get in shape for work now.

729
00:27:34,104 --> 00:27:37,813
Last time, I raced against Hyun Moo. Due to bad blood circulation,

730
00:27:37,814 --> 00:27:39,413
I got a leg cramp, so I lost.

731
00:27:39,414 --> 00:27:42,044
That's why I'm watching my figure now.

732
00:27:42,314 --> 00:27:44,584
People might think that we competed in the Olympics.

733
00:27:45,484 --> 00:27:46,684
It wasn't grand or anything.

734
00:27:47,114 --> 00:27:48,883
We just ran for a bit in front of the MBC building.

735
00:27:48,884 --> 00:27:50,784
How could you get a leg cramp and blame your blood circulation?

736
00:27:50,824 --> 00:27:52,394
I didn't eat the fries. I'm on a diet.

737
00:27:52,954 --> 00:27:55,023
If I keep this diet up,

738
00:27:55,024 --> 00:27:57,093
I'll lose 10kg after 3 weeks.

739
00:27:57,094 --> 00:27:58,234
I'm sure of it.

740
00:27:59,664 --> 00:28:01,034
Gosh, that was good.

741
00:28:02,534 --> 00:28:05,204
I should go and have some desserts.

742
00:28:06,534 --> 00:28:07,543
Thank you.

743
00:28:07,544 --> 00:28:08,803
- You're going for sweets. - Sweets.

744
00:28:08,804 --> 00:28:10,803
- Itaewon has many dessert shops. - Thank you.

745
00:28:10,804 --> 00:28:12,914
There are good dessert shops in Itaewon.

746
00:28:13,714 --> 00:28:14,714
What a nice meal.

747
00:28:14,715 --> 00:28:16,613
(Just then as the sky clears up, his pain eases too.)

748
00:28:16,614 --> 00:28:17,654
My gosh. This is nice.

749
00:28:19,014 --> 00:28:20,454
You look so happy.

750
00:28:22,624 --> 00:28:24,724
- How cute. - How adorable.

751
00:28:25,324 --> 00:28:26,694
- A girl? - What?

752
00:28:26,894 --> 00:28:27,993
- A girl? - Yes.

753
00:28:27,994 --> 00:28:29,194
Yes. My gosh.

754
00:28:30,594 --> 00:28:33,194
Her eyes are so beautiful.

755
00:28:33,334 --> 00:28:34,463
- I see. - Yes.

756
00:28:34,464 --> 00:28:36,034
- Where are you from? - Spain.

757
00:28:36,104 --> 00:28:37,534
- Spain. - Yes, Spain.

758
00:28:38,304 --> 00:28:40,403
You... Can Korean speak English?

759
00:28:40,404 --> 00:28:41,404
What's he saying?

760
00:28:41,405 --> 00:28:43,303
- "Can Korean speak English?" - Okay.

761
00:28:43,304 --> 00:28:44,973
"You Korean can speak English."

762
00:28:44,974 --> 00:28:46,074
Bye.

763
00:28:47,344 --> 00:28:49,743
- Bye. - Bye.

764
00:28:49,744 --> 00:28:51,014
English is all about confidence.

765
00:28:51,114 --> 00:28:52,283
You just have to go for it.

766
00:28:52,284 --> 00:28:53,853
- You need to keep practicing. - Right.

767
00:28:53,854 --> 00:28:55,724
I can make small talk with people now.

768
00:28:57,224 --> 00:28:59,694
(He's confidently roaming around his 5th hometown.)

769
00:29:01,364 --> 00:29:02,494
Gosh, America.

770
00:29:04,164 --> 00:29:05,394
I wonder what he's going to eat.

771
00:29:05,594 --> 00:29:07,194
Where's he going?

772
00:29:10,974 --> 00:29:11,974
- My gosh. - Beyran.

773
00:29:11,975 --> 00:29:13,474
- Oh, right. Yes! - Beyran.

774
00:29:14,034 --> 00:29:15,873
(Beyran?)

775
00:29:15,874 --> 00:29:16,944
You know what?

776
00:29:17,814 --> 00:29:21,483
(The Palm Oil Family had beyran during their seminar in Turkiye.)

777
00:29:21,484 --> 00:29:23,513
This is the ox bone broth.

778
00:29:23,514 --> 00:29:28,684
(They inhaled it as it was spicy ox bone broth.)

779
00:29:29,454 --> 00:29:32,224
(It would be a hit in Korea.)

780
00:29:33,124 --> 00:29:36,294
