1799
01:09:58,332 --> 01:09:59,602
Going uphill is tough.

1800
01:10:00,372 --> 01:10:01,672
He has to run up.

1801
01:10:02,232 --> 01:10:05,002
He would run around the country with four burgers.

1802
01:10:06,172 --> 01:10:08,712
(He quickly reaches the peak!)

1803
01:10:09,272 --> 01:10:10,812
I should try some of that ssanghwatang.

1804
01:10:14,852 --> 01:10:18,822
(Panting)

1805
01:10:20,822 --> 01:10:21,892
I have arrived.

1806
01:10:23,152 --> 01:10:24,262
Gosh, that's great.

1807
01:10:26,622 --> 01:10:28,031
You run to feel that.

1808
01:10:28,032 --> 01:10:30,862
Right. I ran up there to feel that.

1809
01:10:31,432 --> 01:10:33,771
Do you understand the joy you feel at that moment?

1810
01:10:33,772 --> 01:10:34,932
I do.

1811
01:10:35,132 --> 01:10:36,431
It feels annoying when you run out of breath.

1812
01:10:36,432 --> 01:10:39,071
But as for sportsmen like us...

1813
01:10:39,072 --> 01:10:40,241
- "Sportsmen like us." - Well,

1814
01:10:40,242 --> 01:10:42,741
we enjoy that pleasure felt...

1815
01:10:42,742 --> 01:10:44,311
- when our heart rate returns. - You enjoy that?

1816
01:10:44,312 --> 01:10:45,781
- Do you understand that? - Not at all.

1817
01:10:45,782 --> 01:10:46,881
I'm just like you.

1818
01:10:46,882 --> 01:10:48,012
- Right? - We're finally on the same page.

1819
01:10:50,122 --> 01:10:51,252
That was perfect.

1820
01:10:52,422 --> 01:10:54,352
(Feeling refreshed)

1821
01:10:57,322 --> 01:10:58,761
Let's go, SHINee!

1822
01:10:58,762 --> 01:11:01,161
Oh, hello! Thank you!

1823
01:11:01,162 --> 01:11:02,992
The older ladies really like him.

1824
01:11:03,562 --> 01:11:04,702
He looks handsome.

1825
01:11:08,032 --> 01:11:10,007
It's tough to go uphill.

1826
01:11:10,032 --> 01:11:12,501
The slope was higher up than I thought,

1827
01:11:12,502 --> 01:11:13,672
so it was perfect for a workout.

1828
01:11:15,572 --> 01:11:19,282
(Hold on.)

1829
01:11:22,082 --> 01:11:23,212
I should hide it.

1830
01:11:26,822 --> 01:11:28,651
- Is he running in earnest? - No way.

1831
01:11:28,652 --> 01:11:29,691
- Why hide your bag? - He's hiding his bag.

1832
01:11:29,692 --> 01:11:31,921
- He's going to run in earnest. - Where is he going now?

1833
01:11:31,922 --> 01:11:34,032
- He put his bag down. - Where is he going now?

1834
01:11:34,462 --> 01:11:35,532
Great.

1835
01:11:36,132 --> 01:11:38,102
(His body feels much lighter.)

1836
01:11:38,832 --> 01:11:41,032
It's less than 1km.

1837
01:11:42,832 --> 01:11:44,072
I'll go for 5 minutes and 30 seconds.

1838
01:11:44,842 --> 01:11:46,002
He's going for 5 minutes and 30 seconds.

1839
01:11:46,802 --> 01:11:48,042
- An uphill course? - Gosh.

1840
01:11:48,872 --> 01:11:51,012
- Does that make sense? - That's impossible.

1841
01:11:51,342 --> 01:11:54,111
There are quite a lot of steps.

1842
01:11:54,112 --> 01:11:56,482
Going up those stairs at that pace doesn't make sense.

1843
01:11:59,082 --> 01:12:00,192
Get ready.

1844
01:12:03,152 --> 01:12:05,762
(He starts timing his record!)

1845
01:12:06,022 --> 01:12:07,292
Why do this?

1846
01:12:08,532 --> 01:12:11,462
I wanted to check my record.

1847
01:12:14,232 --> 01:12:16,942
(He sprints uphill!)

1848
01:12:17,642 --> 01:12:19,342
Gosh, it's so high up.

1849
01:12:19,702 --> 01:12:20,872
Sean didn't contact you, right?

1850
01:12:21,072 --> 01:12:23,272
- He didn't. - He's scared to contact you.

1851
01:12:24,712 --> 01:12:27,212
(His fiery pace doesn't slow down even while going uphill.)

1852
01:12:27,312 --> 01:12:30,152
You should be enjoying the view. Why run around?

1853
01:12:30,622 --> 01:12:32,782
(Running past)

1854
01:12:34,252 --> 01:12:38,362
(He arrives at his destination in a flash.)

1855
01:12:40,292 --> 01:12:41,391
(He returns to the starting point.)

1856
01:12:41,392 --> 01:12:43,162
Gosh. Did he make it before 5 minutes and 30 seconds?

1857
01:12:43,562 --> 01:12:46,202
- I think he made it. - I think he made it.

1858
01:12:46,862 --> 01:12:47,932
With that pace.

1859
01:12:48,532 --> 01:12:51,501
(That was a clean run.)

1860
01:12:51,502 --> 01:12:52,572
The lunatic with clear eyes.

1861
01:12:53,042 --> 01:12:54,842
(What's my record?)

1862
01:12:55,212 --> 01:12:57,212
I recorded 2 minutes and 13 seconds.

1863
01:12:57,582 --> 01:12:58,981
How long was the course?

1864
01:12:58,982 --> 01:13:01,282
- It was less than 1km. - But it was an uphill course.

1865
01:13:01,652 --> 01:13:04,222
- It looked really high up. - Right.

1866
01:13:04,422 --> 01:13:06,621
After hearing his record, I think he can run a sub-three marathon.

1867
01:13:06,622 --> 01:13:07,821
- Definitely. - He can do that.

1868
01:13:07,822 --> 01:13:10,121
- He can run a sub-three marathon. - What exactly is that?

1869
01:13:10,122 --> 01:13:12,291
It's running a full course in three hours.

1870
01:13:12,292 --> 01:13:14,331
I heard that was a dream record for marathoners.

1871
01:13:14,332 --> 01:13:16,091
It's a dream record...

1872
01:13:16,092 --> 01:13:18,402
for regular runners. I think he can do that.

1873
01:13:18,902 --> 01:13:21,772
(I did it.)

1874
01:13:24,672 --> 01:13:25,672
My bag!

1875
01:13:26,872 --> 01:13:29,912
- Please be stolen. - His bag should be missing.

1876
01:13:31,312 --> 01:13:34,482
- That will be entertainment. - That would make me so happy.

1877
01:13:34,882 --> 01:13:36,581
Unfortunately, our country is safe.

1878
01:13:36,582 --> 01:13:39,221
Right. We live in a safe country.

1879
01:13:39,222 --> 01:13:40,721
No one would take that even after three days.

1880
01:13:40,722 --> 01:13:42,452
- Right. - We live in a great country.

1881
01:13:45,692 --> 01:13:46,722
It's still there.

1882
01:13:47,662 --> 01:13:50,032
(He starts running after getting back his bag.)

1883
01:13:50,362 --> 01:13:53,062
- No way. - No. You don't have to worry.

1884
01:13:55,432 --> 01:13:56,602
It's a chance to lie down!

1885
01:14:02,742 --> 01:14:06,482
(Breathing out)

1886
01:14:07,482 --> 01:14:10,582
(He gets up after a good stretch.)

1887
01:14:11,352 --> 01:14:12,452
This feels amazing.

1888
01:14:13,722 --> 01:14:17,962
(He relaxedly enjoys his favorite scenery.)

1889
01:14:18,522 --> 01:14:20,291
It's my favorite bench.

1890
01:14:20,292 --> 01:14:21,991
- If I sit there, - It seems that way.

1891
01:14:21,992 --> 01:14:23,462
I can see Mount Bukhan well.

1892
01:14:24,232 --> 01:14:26,862
(Getting up)

1893
01:14:29,032 --> 01:14:32,872
(He quickly moves after seeing Mount Bukhan.)

1894
01:14:33,872 --> 01:14:35,342
This feels great.

1895
01:14:37,282 --> 01:14:40,112
(He comes back down to where he started.)

1896
01:14:41,112 --> 01:14:43,952
(He enters the restroom again.)

1897
01:14:44,352 --> 01:14:46,452
He must smell terrible.

1898
01:14:47,522 --> 01:14:49,452
"He must smell terrible."

1899
01:14:52,262 --> 01:14:54,232
(He gets changed into clothes that aren't smelly.)

1900
01:14:55,392 --> 01:14:56,631
- I had a towel, - I bet.

1901
01:14:56,632 --> 01:14:57,801
- so I wiped myself with it. - Let's go.

1902
01:14:57,802 --> 01:14:58,931
There are good towels these days.

1903
01:14:58,932 --> 01:15:00,002
- Right. - Right.

1904
01:15:01,272 --> 01:15:03,532
The ssanghwatang and coffee all went away with my sweat.

1905
01:15:05,102 --> 01:15:06,742
- Where will he go now? - Will he run back home?

1906
01:15:11,482 --> 01:15:14,882
(The place he walks into)

1907
01:15:14,982 --> 01:15:16,381
Hello.

1908
01:15:16,382 --> 01:15:17,652
(A bakery filled with the smell of bread)

1909
01:15:18,122 --> 01:15:19,251
(It smells sweet all around.)

1910
01:15:19,252 --> 01:15:20,651
Gosh, this place looks good.

1911
01:15:20,652 --> 01:15:21,991
This place has great bread.

1912
01:15:21,992 --> 01:15:23,691
- The matcha one looks good. - Right.

1913
01:15:23,692 --> 01:15:26,522
This is my favorite bakery.

1914
01:15:26,962 --> 01:15:30,192
I would like to get two pieces of Salt Bread.

1915
01:15:30,832 --> 01:15:32,531
- One Palmier Carre... - Palmier Carre?

1916
01:15:32,532 --> 01:15:34,401
And one Salt.

1917
01:15:34,402 --> 01:15:35,931
- Right. - Will you get four in total?

1918
01:15:35,932 --> 01:15:37,541
No. I'll be getting more.

1919
01:15:37,542 --> 01:15:39,102
Gosh, he's getting a lot.

1920
01:15:39,402 --> 01:15:41,312
I'll get two pieces of Salt.

1921
01:15:41,712 --> 01:15:43,542
Two pieces of Salt Bread and two pieces of Salt.

1922
01:15:44,142 --> 01:15:46,942
I'll get two Palmier Carres as well.

1923
01:15:47,312 --> 01:15:48,481
Also...

1924
01:15:48,482 --> 01:15:49,652
(He gets a generous amount of bread.)

1925
01:15:49,812 --> 01:15:51,522
One Almond...

1926
01:15:51,882 --> 01:15:53,222
and the Ham and Cheese.

1927
01:15:53,552 --> 01:15:54,721
He must be going somewhere.

1928
01:15:54,722 --> 01:15:56,291
- It must be for his trainers. - Right.

1929
01:15:56,292 --> 01:15:57,321
- As a gift? - Right.

1930
01:15:57,322 --> 01:15:59,092
He only meets his trainers.

1931
01:16:00,092 --> 01:16:02,631
- I barely get to see him either. - They're the only ones he meets.

1932
01:16:02,632 --> 01:16:04,662
- Thank you. - Thank you.

1933
01:16:05,032 --> 01:16:06,802
- Goodbye. - Thank you. Enjoy the bread.

1934
01:16:09,402 --> 01:16:11,442
- He's not eating them. - He must be eating at home.

1935
01:16:12,472 --> 01:16:13,472
(Where is he heading to with both hands full of snacks?)

1936
01:16:13,472 --> 01:16:14,472
Where is he going?

1937
01:16:15,674 --> 01:16:16,733
He got some coffee as well.

1938
01:16:16,734 --> 01:16:18,044
Right.

1939
01:16:18,174 --> 01:16:19,244
I figured it out.

1940
01:16:19,744 --> 01:16:20,943
He must be meeting someone.

1941
01:16:20,944 --> 01:16:21,944
Right.

1942
01:16:24,414 --> 01:16:25,584
(Hall 3 Ticket Office)

1943
01:16:25,944 --> 01:16:26,984
Is he watching a performance?

1944
01:16:27,214 --> 01:16:29,084
He's been watching a lot of plays these days.

1945
01:16:29,184 --> 01:16:30,984
I see.

1946
01:16:31,924 --> 01:16:35,154
(He opens the door with an excited heart.)

1947
01:16:37,894 --> 01:16:39,794
(He arrives at the theater.)

1948
01:16:39,824 --> 01:16:43,263
This is a theater in Daehangno...

1949
01:16:43,264 --> 01:16:45,264
where I am currently performing.

1950
01:16:45,804 --> 01:16:48,234
- So this is before the performance? - Right.

1951
01:16:50,574 --> 01:16:52,974
(The stage that is ready for the performance...)

1952
01:16:53,074 --> 01:16:55,944
(is filled with items that build up the setting.)

1953
01:16:57,514 --> 01:16:58,914
I performed for around two weeks.

1954
01:16:59,314 --> 01:17:00,654
- At that time? - Right.

1955
01:17:01,554 --> 01:17:02,584
Hi.

1956
01:17:03,524 --> 01:17:04,554
You're here early.

1957
01:17:05,984 --> 01:17:07,224
Come down and have some of this.

1958
01:17:07,924 --> 01:17:10,264
He brought it for the staff.

1959
01:17:11,994 --> 01:17:17,004
(He goes backstage naturally.)

1960
01:17:18,864 --> 01:17:23,474
- Hello! - Hey, MINHO!

1961
01:17:23,844 --> 01:17:26,544
- I've come with both hands full! - Gosh!

1962
01:17:27,414 --> 01:17:30,384
- Gosh. - I brought bread and drinks.

1963
01:17:31,984 --> 01:17:33,914
- Gosh. - It's Lee Sang Yun!

1964
01:17:36,054 --> 01:17:37,584
- Byoung Cheol! - It's Byoung Cheol.

1965
01:17:37,624 --> 01:17:38,984
Mr. Catastrophe!

1966
01:17:41,754 --> 01:17:44,294
(Mr. Catastrophe)

1967
01:17:45,394 --> 01:17:47,894
(Actor Kim Byoung Cheol)

1968
01:17:48,594 --> 01:17:51,564
(Soft charisma in mildness)

1969
01:17:52,304 --> 01:17:55,604
(Actor Lee Sang Yun)

1970
01:17:55,934 --> 01:17:57,444
Kim Byoung Cheol...

1971
01:17:57,604 --> 01:17:59,103
and Lee Sang Yun.

1972
01:17:59,104 --> 01:18:00,344
Since I'm the youngest,

1973
01:18:00,714 --> 01:18:02,344
they treat me well with whatever I do.

1974
01:18:02,614 --> 01:18:04,484
They listen to everything I say.

1975
01:18:05,614 --> 01:18:08,084
I thought that I should do well as the youngest.

1976
01:18:08,354 --> 01:18:09,813
That was why I went to support them.

1977
01:18:09,814 --> 01:18:10,954
(I went to support my seniors.)

1978
01:18:10,984 --> 01:18:13,754
Sang Yun and I are doubles.

1979
01:18:13,924 --> 01:18:16,254
Byoung Cheol is a different character.

1980
01:18:16,494 --> 01:18:18,324
Was Byoung Cheol double cast as well?

1981
01:18:18,394 --> 01:18:20,593
Yes. Byoung Cheol...

1982
01:18:20,594 --> 01:18:22,194
is double cast with Park Geun Hyung.

1983
01:18:22,264 --> 01:18:23,634
- Park Geun Hyung? - Yes.

1984
01:18:24,604 --> 01:18:27,374
I brought three for you.

1985
01:18:27,604 --> 01:18:29,504
- Awesome. - Choose from them.

1986
01:18:30,034 --> 01:18:32,574
I didn't feel like having coffee for some reason.

1987
01:18:32,644 --> 01:18:34,713
- Really? - I must've known you were coming.

1988
01:18:34,714 --> 01:18:36,544
Fortunately, he didn't have any coffee.

1989
01:18:36,714 --> 01:18:37,914
- That was a relief. - Right.

1990
01:18:38,584 --> 01:18:39,644
Coffee for you.

1991
01:18:40,284 --> 01:18:41,884
(The youngest delivers coffee to everyone.)

1992
01:18:42,784 --> 01:18:43,784
Byoung Cheol.

1993
01:18:44,084 --> 01:18:46,653
I got something for you.

1994
01:18:46,654 --> 01:18:48,793
You should brush your teeth again.

1995
01:18:48,794 --> 01:18:49,924
(Thank you, Youngest.)

1996
01:18:50,054 --> 01:18:52,764
I had this and it was really good.

1997
01:18:53,294 --> 01:18:55,794
I thought it would be perfect for Byoung Cheol.

1998
01:18:56,434 --> 01:18:59,004
- I bought ssanghwatang. - I was going to mention that!

1999
01:19:00,274 --> 01:19:02,333
I was going to ask if it was ssanghwatang.

2000
01:19:02,334 --> 01:19:03,573
It's good for the throat.

2001
01:19:03,574 --> 01:19:05,474
- It suits Byoung Cheol. - Right.

2002
01:19:05,744 --> 01:19:06,844
Did you not work out today?

2003
01:19:07,044 --> 01:19:08,314
I worked out during the day.

2004
01:19:08,474 --> 01:19:09,474
What did you do today?

2005
01:19:09,475 --> 01:19:11,384
Today,

2006
01:19:11,944 --> 01:19:13,484
I did something like CrossFit.

2007
01:19:13,854 --> 01:19:16,284
- It's the circuit? - Right. I did that slightly.

2008
01:19:16,754 --> 01:19:18,084
And I did two laps in Naksan Park.

2009
01:19:18,184 --> 01:19:19,684
I went back and forth.

2010
01:19:20,024 --> 01:19:21,154
That was a brief workout?

2011
01:19:22,224 --> 01:19:23,524
- Right. - That was a brief workout?

2012
01:19:23,824 --> 01:19:25,393
- Gosh, you brought bread as well. - Right.

2013
01:19:25,394 --> 01:19:26,523
He brought us bread as well.

2014
01:19:26,524 --> 01:19:28,334
- Thank you. - Don't mention it.

2015
01:19:28,564 --> 01:19:30,263
- Do you have your own? - He's good to the older guys.

2016
01:19:30,264 --> 01:19:31,364
Right.

2017
01:19:31,404 --> 01:19:32,833
- He knows how to be loved. - They all took great care of me...

2018
01:19:32,834 --> 01:19:34,603
during rehearsals.

2019
01:19:34,604 --> 01:19:36,403
They take good care of you because you treat them so well.

2020
01:19:36,404 --> 01:19:38,744
They take good care of you because you do well.

2021
01:19:39,274 --> 01:19:40,774
What did you do in the morning?

2022
01:19:40,914 --> 01:19:42,044
Today,

2023
01:19:42,944 --> 01:19:44,784
I was with KSOC...

2024
01:19:45,044 --> 01:19:46,614
as I became an ambassador.

2025
01:19:46,784 --> 01:19:48,083
(I became an ambassador.)

2026
01:19:48,084 --> 01:19:49,553
I went to the appointment ceremony.

2027
01:19:49,554 --> 01:19:51,654
- That suits you perfectly. - He's an athlete now.

2028
01:19:52,384 --> 01:19:56,424
He became an ambassador of KSOC today.

2029
01:19:56,594 --> 01:19:57,794
Congratulations, MINHO.

2030
01:19:59,024 --> 01:20:00,463
He doesn't even look surprised.

2031
01:20:00,464 --> 01:20:01,534
He knows him too well.

2032
01:20:01,594 --> 01:20:03,163
Will you get paid regularly?

2033
01:20:03,164 --> 01:20:05,534
- No. It's just an honorary title. - "Paid regularly?"

2034
01:20:05,604 --> 01:20:06,864
- An honorary title. - Right.

2035
01:20:06,964 --> 01:20:10,773
I will be sharing with everyone that exercising is great.

2036
01:20:10,774 --> 01:20:11,843
I see.

2037
01:20:11,844 --> 01:20:15,374
Just like how you work out before getting on stage.

2038
01:20:15,674 --> 01:20:18,384
- He works out really hard. - He's intense.

2039
01:20:19,044 --> 01:20:21,483
I got so surprised. He kept doing the plank.

2040
01:20:21,484 --> 01:20:24,584
I got really surprised.

2041
01:20:25,654 --> 01:20:28,954
You three all look very close. Were you always that close?

2042
01:20:29,754 --> 01:20:33,463
Sang Yun made a great effort...

2043
01:20:33,464 --> 01:20:35,233
to make all of us get along.

2044
01:20:35,234 --> 01:20:38,464
Byoung Cheol was actually a very shy person,

2045
01:20:38,604 --> 01:20:41,104
but we got very close as he broke the ice for us.

2046
01:20:41,874 --> 01:20:44,274
- Byoung Cheol. - Have this, Byoung Cheol.

2047
01:20:45,004 --> 01:20:46,874
I bought ssanghwatang for you.

2048
01:20:48,474 --> 01:20:51,884
You seemed to have a bad throat for a while.

2049
01:20:52,884 --> 01:20:54,613
He's really good to the older ones.

2050
01:20:54,614 --> 01:20:56,614
Right. He knows how to be loved.

2051
01:20:56,854 --> 01:20:58,353
- Really? - Yes.

2052
01:20:58,354 --> 01:20:59,824
(Touched)

2053
01:21:02,324 --> 01:21:03,653
I bought it for you.

2054
01:21:03,654 --> 01:21:06,024
(Acting cute)

2055
01:21:06,694 --> 01:21:08,534
It's healthy and is good for your throat.

2056
01:21:09,234 --> 01:21:10,603
You should stay healthy.

2057
01:21:10,604 --> 01:21:12,064
- Right. - Right.

2058
01:21:12,234 --> 01:21:13,664
MINHO got it for you.

2059
